    "turn_text": "If we had a real press corps Meaning that people that call themselves journalists view their role as getting the facts, speaking, speaking truth to power, holding power accountable, all the things that journalists pretend they are that they are not overwhelmingly, not all of them, but most vast majority of them. If we had a real press corps, you know what question would be asked of Democrats? Not what do you think about Trump's handling of the border? No, no, no. What should be asked of all the Democrat candidates for president so that the American people can really know what's going on here? What's going to be asked is what should be done about the border? What actions would you as president take that are different from and better than whatever Trump has done so far? That would be very interesting, wouldn't it? Because Democrats, their first instinct, and this is, it's a form of a, it's almost like Tourette's that they can't control it. There's a reactionary feeling that they have whenever they have an opportunity to talk about anything that they can relate to Trump, it's just Trump bad, Trump bad, orange man bad that they cannot help it. And that would be their first reaction is that Trump is terrible and he's done all these horrible things. And oh, here, here's Joe Biden doing exactly that. Play 22.",
