    "turn_text": "Okay, these people also all go after him all the time. I think Democrats are just still upset that now there's a Republican president that doesn't think that manners dictate that he just sits there and takes it quietly all the time, while Pelosi trashes him, Pelosi wishes that he was put in prison, knowing that that was going to make its way into the press. But yeah, he's supposed to just sit there quietly, not supposed to have an opinion about this. What is Joe Biden's opinion on the border? Notice they like talking about Trump separates people because they always wanted a family. The one thing where they've been able to get this administration to back down and change course is on family separation at the border. And so you'll hear a lot more of that. That is where they've managed to get Trump to change course on something because the outrage over that was, oh my gosh, it was a level, it was a level 11 out of 10. I mean, people were completely freaked out about this. Meanwhile, across the country, people are separated from their children all the time. Whenever they're put in prison, that happens constantly. It's a sad thing, but it is a reality of life for a lot of Americans. But if you don't believe the crossing in the country illegally is a crime, well, then you don't think there should be any punishment for that crime. That's what Democrats should be asked. Is illegal immigration wrong? They'll probably say yes, because they know if they say no, then it would be, well, why don't you just say then that you're an open borders party? So they'll say, yes, legal immigration is wrong, but then they should be asked, why is it wrong? What is the problem with illegal immigration? They just say, well, we have law and say, okay, but if there's no downside, then why do we have that law? You can't let them escape with just the pretense of legalism, right? Oh, well, it's bad because there's a law against it. Well, why is there a law against it? Because if it's not bad for any reason beyond the law, we should just repeal that law. they won't be able to answer the democrats i've tried this with many democrats and they get very flustered and very angry but but but uh... well they they do not cause any crime they're not a drain on public resources they do the jobs americans won't do that you know we're a nation of immigrants there the same as our uh... you know our parents and grandparents who came here legally etc etc i mean these are all the the democrats talking points Where's the downside? They don't admit there is any downside. So shouldn't they have to then admit that they are an open borders, open borders political party? If we had a real press corps, that would be raised. That would be clear, but we don't. We have a bunch of Democrat lackeys, generally from a very mediocre intellectual backgrounds who run around parroting each other and patting each other on the backs for their bravery in front of one another. But Lindsey Graham understands that we are at a breaking point at the border and it's no longer okay to sit back and allow the status quo. It hasn't been okay for months, but now it's really getting out of control. Here's what the Senator has to say. Play 24.",
