    "turn_text": "The time will tell is the massive gamble. It may be really in some ways the biggest gamble of his presidency because he's gone against the consensus. People have been saying, Oh, you know, trade war and this is terrible and you can't do this. Well, if we get a real deal with China in place, which probably won't happen till after Trump's reelection, which I am not, I'm not getting lackadaisical about. I'm not, I'm not thinking that it's already done, but feeling good about it right now for sure. But if Trump gets a deal with China, then he will have managed to defy 90% plus of the trade and econ experts out there and the chattering class and all the people that go on TV to talk about Wall Street, all the bonds today are up. They're down. The stock price is up. It's down. One thing that's funny is if you want to hear people that are usually just blathering on about nonsense, that make political pundits look really smart by comparison, turn on some of the financial news networks that are out there and just see if they're, yeah, you know, a fear of a dollar and the gold and the yen and the this and the dead and that's what made the, you know, Market go up or down, they have no idea. The people I know who know the market say, these guys have no idea, they just gotta say something. They're there to convey the information about the stock price and they say all this other stuff around it to make it seem like, they're almost, they're like sports announcers without the entertainment value added. You know, you wanna know what the score is, you wanna know what's going on. You don't really need to get that in depth about how the person viewing it seems to think that the person playing the game is thinking about playing the game. But I really do think that Trump on China is gonna be, I think that he's got a real shot. I'm not gonna tell you it's likely that the Chinese government has managed to defy international pressure and expectations for a long time. But yo