erson, but it is the movement. It's the agenda. It's not the individual. I'm not disappointed when Trump says something that I'm like, Oh, he, you know, he got a little too personal there or not because I know that that's what he does. And it's he's not perfect, but I don't expect him to be. So at least more admits that because you often have all these evangelical Christians, they don't even know the Trump's, no, they know, but they also want to fight her for their side and their freedom. And they don't want somebody who's just going to meekly go off and say, well, you know, maybe one day the left will come and see the light. That's not going to happen. so that part of it he gets right but then also on political correctness as a a cancer on the left it's absolutely the case Political correctness is completely out of control across the country. I don't even know what's acceptable anymore. And I can tell you that I've had a few incidents here or there with maybe perhaps, you know, I won't get into the specifics of it, but where someone said, oh, you can't say that or a buck, you know, you'll get in trouble for that. And I just look at them and say, why? the things that i say i stand behind a hundred percent of there's nothing that i've said that uh... uh... on on radio or on twitter is usually what gets people into that's what gets me a little bit of hot water sometimes because i have to throw out you know twitter is is a place where sure you can communicate but it's really a place where it's just hot takes it just people taking swings at the other side and see what what resonates and when you take swings people get upset about it they get upset they say very nasty things about you. Although I do like the, the intelligence test that Twitter provides, which is that anybody, especially a journal, believe it or not, they do this too, who in response to something I say about politics or life or whatever comes at me with, your name is stupid. This is a thing that only stupid people think and would laugh at. This is something that only a true moron goes, I don't like your name. Your name is funny. Hey, you know, this is something that you come across with leftists all the time. But they have a childish approach to debate. And one of the reasons they're so reliant on political correctness is that it's a means of shutting down points of view that they don't like. you can always find some some tie-in to a a politically correct narrative on any major issue especially with the intersection left these days there's a way to say you know if nothing else will book your opinion doesn't count because you're a a cisgender white christian male well that i guess that i i'm my opinion shouldn't matter anymore then and if i disagree with that notion then i'm a bad person So there are ways to weaponize political correctness in any discussion, in any debate, and it is done with a deep disingenuousness on a regular basis. So Mar recognizes that and I think he deserves credit for recognizing that. He's also somebody who has been able to get, you know, the fact that he thinks political correctness is too much, given that he always has the good graces of the left to go back to because he's with them on 90% of stuff, 95% of stuff. But with today's left, if you're with them 90% of the time, but you break with them on 5% and 5%, let's say you're either agnostic or in the middle on, you get on the wrong part of the news cycle and they'll want to crush you. They'll want to take you down. They'll want to finish you off just to make an example to the others. It's madness. a normal healthy functioning adult does not know cannot know what the true here here's a here's an example i'll give you an example like i i won't say what organization i can tell you this it didn't happen as a result of it has nothing to do with my radio show or or my podcast or where the companies involved in that but a at a previous employer i was censured internally for referring to a female