    "turn_text": "There's a lot of that going on. Back to political correctness though. yeah i was told that i couldn't say that a female politician was attractive and that and that uh... initially i was told that i had to make an apology which i refused uh... and then i was told that it would be handled but the people involved the uh... at least one young woman uh... decided to make it make a real issue of it and this was the real kicker thought that for that crime i should be fired and anything short of that was insufficient punishment now to this i say uh... especially in the era of bearded i'm gonna throw down buck i don't really care anymore uh... that was kind of funny right all i'm gonna get fired from that job and my some of you're probably already figured out what you are talking about that's okay uh... we don't have to name names or name organizations but i just thought myself here's somebody who is so really uh... indecent and so nasty she doesn't know who i am i've never met this person by the way still never never well had had one interaction with the person uh... that was on set and in front of a dozen people was completely professional and normal uh... never uh... net no other interaction whatsoever and the comment about a track in this had nothing to do with her it had to do with a politician a public figure and the comment was she's attractive uh... the public figure and i just i thought to myself this is where intersectional feminists have have gone now uh... they are they're actually cruel and there's a nastiness that's only possible because they're so deeply unhappy and so vicious and they're so in sconce in this politically correct nonsense you know what if i was about to uh... proposed to my fiance saving up for rain or saving up for a house what if i had three kids And that was my only means of sustaining myself. I was supposed to get... I should be fired for my job for saying that a woman in public life is attractive. It didn't sound like a sexy babe with a great, you know, something, something. I just said attractive. Oh no, I should be fired for that. that to me was a particularly noteworthy instance of this politically correct nonsense run amok because it was it was taken somewhat seriously by the authority that they had to go through all the motions and i was i was having none of it on the go through the motions is ridiculous You want me to, you want me to act like I'm, I'm going to be what? And we're going to investigate the comment, but what do you think this is? If apologizing isn't enough, and the only, the only thing that would satisfy the professional bloodlust of this vicious little harpy that wants people fired for a comment that is completely innocuous and, you know, I'm, I'm to take this seriously. I'm to take this seriously. Wow. Okay. That's the world we live in now, right? And that's certainly the media landscape, isn't it? That's certainly the situation we find ourselves in across much of corporate America, that unreasonable demands are now the norm, that unreasonable political correctness is expected. And just as is the case with any true tyranny, which listens to this show now, a true tyranny is where you don't know what ease in is not acceptable because it changes all the time, right? It's the capricious enforcement of ever changing laws and rules, not the very strict enforcement of rules, because at least you know what to do when the rules are very strict. You can break them or not. People have had enough. I've had enough. I have had enough with it. And there will be consequences for those of us that decide that this is too much and we don't want to live this anymore. There won't really be consequences for Bill Maher. And so that's why there needs to be some. Well, on the one hand, I'm saying, well, we need to give him credit. Sure. But he will always be welcome back on the left on the right. They want us erased. They want to salt the earth of our lives and our careers when we transgress the political correct, politically correct gods, so to speak. And it's just wrong. It is just wrong. And Trump for all of his flaws, although he's been a darn good president, but for all of his flaws personally, he's a warrior on this issue and is more effective on it than anyone else. And you know why? Because he will not bend the knee. And that's really what it takes. It takes someone who won't bend the knee and who can't be destroyed because he won't, because he won't bend the knee. It's a magical thing that Trump has, has managed and it has real implications, real ramifications in the war for freedom of conscience, freedom of thought, free speech. Just the fact that Trump won't bend to the dictates of the politically correct left is a major victory in and of itself.",
