    "turn_text": "I'm not trying to do some Bill Maher lovefest today, but he's right again. This gets lost in all the discussions. All this gets lost and it's not an accident. And then all the discussions about 2016 and Russia collusion and, and obstruction and all this stuff. Hillary was a terrible candidate. Hillary brazenly. I mean, just men with the mendacity that she displayed with the lies that she told. I mean, the way that she was willing to just look the American people in the eye and say, you know, oh, there's nothing to this email. There was nothing classified. There's nothing. She lied and lied and lied and the media were just covering for her at every turn. The same media that Nog was, why don't you more upset about Trump when he lies? Well, what is Trump lying about exactly? Is that he's the greatest and the smartest and the best? We can make our own decisions about that. We don't consider that to be a lie. What's he lying about that he makes the best deals? You know, they always talk about all of Trump's lies. And then I say, what's the lie? Exactly. And then they say something that's usually an opinion or usually them taking an exaggeration or a bit of salesmanship from Trump word for word literally, which they would never do with any other candidate, but they love to do it with Trump. Hillary lies about big stuff. Hillary lies about things that matter. And she also clearly obstructed justice. And that tells you everything you need to know about the people involved in the email investigation of Hillary, who by the way, were the same people that DOJ involved in the Trump-Russia collusion force. Why was she destroying devices? Why was she deleting emails after they were under subpoena? she was destroying evidence that's what that is if if Hillary Clinton were a run-of-the-mill accounting firm and she had done this to exact same stuff that she did in any kind of a federal you know financial fraud investigation she'd be facing twenty years in prison i'm not exaggerating the the statutes that exist under i think it's dot frank for destruction of evidence in a financial crimes case if they have draconian penalties Hillary didn't suffer any of that though. It wasn't even an issue. She was never going to be charged. You want to talk about above the law? They just ignored Hillary breaking the law entirely. They didn't even put it. really before a serious investigator. The whole point of the investigation was to make the thing go away. It was a sham. It was a scam. The whole investigation of Hillary's emails was never serious. It was a box checking exercise that was not going to lead to charges. And unlike Trump, she wasn't the president. She was just a person. A person who was lying and a person who was exposed for what she really was. She was a terrible candidate. She broke the law. She broke the law with the obstruction. She broke the law with, I mean, that's classic. That's textbook obstruction. It's destruction of evidence.",
